This fixture exercises phpc's deterministic direct-variable
`mysqli_stmt_bind_param()` refresh when `mysqli_stmt_execute()` is invoked
through `call_user_func()` or positional `call_user_func_array()`. System PHP
requires a real initialized MySQLi connection and by-reference mysqlnd
parameter binding; phpc re-reads direct variables in the current scope for
exact known placeholder SQL shapes. It does not implement true by-reference
aliasing, cross-scope reference cells, array parameter execution, mutation SQL,
broad SQL execution, host database state, PHP warning/error fidelity, or native
database lowering.
